<title>UK: EIB adds 300 million Ecu to April 2004 bond.</title>
<headline>EIB adds 300 million Ecu to April 2004 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 1.3 billion Ecu from 1.0 billion Ecu, joint lead managers Paribas Capital Markets, CDC and SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT   *1.3 BLN ECU   COUPON     5.25	MATURITY    15.APR.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.606    PAY DATE  **05.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  30 BP     LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> NOTES	FUNGIBLE INTO EURO</p>
<p>	     *LAUNCHED ORIGINALLY FOR 1.0 BILLION ECU ON 15.APR.97</p>
<p>	    **PLUS 21 DAYS ACCRUED INTEREST</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   GOV LAW    ENG	 MGT/UND    30 BP</p>
<p> SPREAD     -1 BP</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
